{"name": "mcdaniel-2019", "title": "Replicating McDaniel et al. 2019 (sepsis in BioGears) on BioGears 8.2.0", "campaign_docs": [], "description": "Three studies on the biogears_sepsis composite. Its treatment parameter runs the paper's protocols (viva_biogears.protocols, TreatmentController). The progression arms run 48 h from t = 0; as in the paper, every treatment arm starts from the severe infection's state saved at 44 h (viva_biogears/states/StandardMale@severe-infection-44h.xml) and runs 8-20 h. mcdaniel-2019-sepsis/run.py runs the same arms outside the workbench, and analyze.py draws the paper's figures. Fig 8 (inflammation parameter changes) needs changes inside BioGears and is out of scope.\n", "lead": "", "at_a_glance": [], "how_to_read": [], "glossary": [], "biological_story": "", "question": "Does BioGears 8.2.0, driven through viva-biogears, reproduce McDaniel et al. (2019): sepsis progression by infection severity (Figs 4-7), the fluid challenge and antibiotic (Figs 9-10), and the REFRESH resuscitation protocols, on time and delayed (Figs 11-13)?\n", "hypothesis": "The progression follows the paper up to hypotension, but on 8.2.0 the severe arm does not reach septic shock by 48 h; the treatments act as the paper describes: the challenge restores volume, piperacillin exceeds the MIC and lowers the pathogen, both REFRESH protocols reach the goals with the experimental one using less fluid, and a 12 h delay costs more fluid.\n", "object_of_evaluation": null, "status": "planned", "effective_status": "planning", "origin_repo": null, "read_only": false, "expert_docs": [], "acceptance_criteria": [{"study": "mcdaniel-2019-sepsis", "behavior": "severity-orders-the-response"}, {"study": "mcdaniel-2019-sepsis", "behavior": "only-severe-decompensates"}, {"study": "mcdaniel-2019-sepsis", "behavior": "severe-hypovolemia"}, {"study": "mcdaniel-2019-treatment", "behavior": "protocol-is-delivered"}, {"study": "mcdaniel-2019-treatment", "behavior": "challenge-restores-vo